==Strategy==
Despite the extreme prevalence of zombies and Wild Doge in this stage, their relatively low strength magnification mean they aren't as threatening, but they do deny or discourage the use of less disposable backliners and Cumulus Gallus/Lophiiformes Angaburu only complicate matters further. More often than not, you'll have to prepare for an endurance battle and take out the nasty Alien pushers as well.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]]: The Zombies are so weak that not even specialists are needed for them, but Cat Chief notably helps the most if you need one. Its [[Massive Damage]] to Zombies, Zombie Killer and Soulstrike all help in wiping them out, and while its [[Behemoth Slayer]] is not useful in general due to its very low range, it easily obliterates Formicidaean Ariant while its occasional [[Mini-Wave]]s can snipe Angaburu, exploiting this enemy's low health.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Courier's good stats and Behemoth Slayer are both of use here, countering many of the peons well and especially the tanky Piggicus as well as the dangerous Wild Doge. If positioned properly, they can even snipe Cumulus Gallus without coming under fire, quickly deplete Ariant's health and deal some serious damage to Angaburu.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Can Can's high stats for a melee unit makes it particularly suited for dealing with the stronger peons like Scissoroos, especially with Speed Up and Extra Money Talents for an easier startoff.
*[[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Awakened Urs]]: Though the presence of Zombies would usually prohibit the use of traditional backliners, the only respawning Zombie is Zroco, who shouldn't be too threatening. As the fight is expected to drag on, Urs can be used at the end where you're left slowly chipping away Cumulus Gallus, where their Behemoth Slayer ability can be put to great use.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[EVA Unit-01 (Uber Rare Cat)|EVA Unit-01]]: One of the best units for the stage, EVA Unit-01's assortment of anti-Alien and anti-Zombie abilities can easily trivialize threats of both traits, able to tank them (specifically Angaburu's [[Mini-Surge]]) and deal lots of damage at a safe distance while finishing the Zombies for good. As it outranges all enemies, you only really need to worry about the Wild Doges.
*[[Sharpshooter Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Nighthunter Saki]]: This is an ideal stage for this specialist, her evolved form targets Alien and Zombie and has [[Zombie Killer]]. Due to the large amount of peons, money is not an issue on this stage, allowing Saki's low cooldown to actually be relevant despite her high cost.
*Any [[Frontline Assault IRON LEGION (Gacha Event)|IRON LEGION]] Uber: Due to their assortment of anti-Zombie abilities, almost any of them will do well here, though the damage-focused ones are obviously the most useful.

